        "title": "fix(qqbot): clean up token refresh sleep abort listener",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where the QQBot access token refresh loop could keep adding abort listeners to a long-lived signal between refresh sleeps.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe refresh sleep helper now removes its abort listener when the sleep resolves normally, while keeping the existing abort behavior when shutdown cancels the loop. The change is limited to token refresh timing cleanup.\n\nThis is an AI-assisted contribution prepared for Alix-007.\n\n## User Impact\n\nLong-running QQBot sessions avoid accumulating redundant abort listeners during repeated token refresh cycles.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs extensions/qqbot/src/engine/api/token.test.ts`\n- Result: 1 test file passed, 8 tests passed.\n- `git diff --check HEAD^ HEAD --`\n- Result: passed.\n",
